   "unmapped": [
    "Reward function evolves by Markov model f_{t+1} = sqrt(1-eps) f_t + sqrt(eps) g_{t+1}, g_t i.i.d. GP(0,k); eps is the variation rate",
    "The learner knows the variation rate eps and kernel hyperparameters",
    "Regret is measured against the maximizer of f_t at each round (dynamic regret)"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "Letting $g_1,g_2,\\dotsc$ be independent random functions on $D$ with $g_i \\sim \\GP(0,k)$, the reward functions are modeled as follows: f_1(x) = g_1(x), f_{t+1}(x) = \\sqrt{1 - \\epsilon}\\,f_{t}(x) +  \\sqrt{\\epsilon}\\,g_{t+1}(x) ... Then the instantaneous regret we incur at time $t$ is $r_t = f_t(x^*_t) - f_t(x_t)$."
  },
